# Skills maintenance

When you **add or materially change** a product feature, update agent memory in the **same task** (or PR) — do not leave skills stale.

## When this applies

- New UI surface, server action, socket event, migration, or route
- Changed data model, RLS, or shared types for a feature area
- New conventions (tokens, hooks, file locations) others will copy
- Removed or renamed behavior that skills still document

Skip for typo fixes, pure refactors with no behavior change, or one-off scripts.

## What to update

| Change area | Update |
|-------------|--------|
| Any feature | Matching skill `SKILL.md` + `reference.md` if present |
| Room / listing / social | `studyverce-rooms` |
| Post-its / tasks | `studyverce-post-it-notes` |
| Dashboard | `studyverce-dashboard` |
| Cross-cutting layout or commands | `studyverce-overview.mdc`, root `AGENTS.md` |
| File-specific patterns | Relevant `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` (e.g. `room-features.mdc`) |
| New feature domain | New skill under `.cursor/skills/<name>/` + row in `.cursor/skills/README.md` |

## Minimum doc updates per feature change

1. **SKILL.md** — workflow steps, pitfalls, and “where to look” for the new/changed behavior.
2. **reference.md** — tables (routes, components, actions, migrations, socket events).
3. **AGENTS.md** — “Where to look” row if a new primary file or feature name.
4. **Rule `.mdc`** — short bullet if the change affects globs that rule covers.

## Skill frontmatter

Refresh the skill `description` in YAML when scope grows (so auto-routing still picks the right skill).

## Checklist before finishing

- [ ] Read the relevant skill **before** coding; update it **after** if behavior or files changed.
- [ ] `reference.md` lists new files, actions, migrations, or events.
- [ ] `AGENTS.md` / `studyverce-overview.mdc` updated if the feature is user-visible or cross-cutting.
- [ ] No documented steps contradict the current code.

See `.cursor/skills/README.md` for the skill index.
